  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus of mass $M+\\Delta m$ is at rest and decays into two daughter nuclei of equal mass $\\frac{M}{2}$ each. Speed of light is $\\mathrm{c}$.\n40. The binding energy per nucleon for the parent nucleus is $E_1$ and that for the daughter nuclei is $E_2$. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Kwgbe",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{E}_2=2 \\mathrm{E}_1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IX5Ps",
      "text": "\n$E_1>E_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FcS5L",
      "text": "\n$E_2>E_1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "BQhJA",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{E}_1=2 \\mathrm{E}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "After decay, the daughter nuclei will be more stable hence binding energy per nucleon will be more than that of their parent nucleus.",
    "image": null
  },
